1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:07,036
Docket keeps invoice expectations and payment evidence in one review desk.

2
00:00:07,036 --> 00:00:14,163
This is a real Sepolia transfer with an illustrative invoice, not customer
work.

3
00:00:14,163 --> 00:00:21,344
The expected recipient and exact amount stay beside the source
transaction.

4
00:00:21,344 --> 00:00:28,466
A random salt keeps the invoice fingerprint from revealing private
details.

5
00:00:28,466 --> 00:00:37,020
First, read the source receipt and compare the transfer with the
expectation.

6
00:00:37,020 --> 00:00:44,689
The call succeeded and the recipient and amount match. Inclusion is still
unchecked.

7
00:00:44,689 --> 00:00:55,784
Now Attestcoin builds a proof and Creditcoin checks transaction inclusion.

8
00:00:55,784 --> 00:01:03,507
Inclusion is verified. It is separate from payment matching and invoice
ownership.

9
00:01:03,507 --> 00:01:11,552
A public registry write is a separate step. It is still waiting for free
testnet gas.

10
00:01:11,552 --> 00:01:18,584
Leave a note describing exactly what the evidence supports.

11
00:01:18,584 --> 00:01:26,140
Reviewed requires a successful receipt, an exact transfer match and real
inclusion.

12
00:01:26,140 --> 00:01:33,177
Save the decision with its note so the next review has context.

13
00:01:33,177 --> 00:01:40,733
The public export leaves out invoice text, the salt and reviewer notes.

14
00:01:40,733 --> 00:01:48,300
A separate private bundle is for a chosen reviewer or your own backup.

15
00:01:48,300 --> 00:01:55,531
Earlier network checks stay in the export. A new check does not rewrite
them.

16
00:01:55,531 --> 00:02:03,178
The saved record survives a reload. The private data stays in this
browser.

17
00:02:03,178 --> 00:02:10,303
Docket makes the evidence clear before a team marks a payment record
reviewed.
